#      string "{max_pct}", substituted with the configured CPU ceiling, or
#      "{deepest_pct}", the same ceiling but at most DEEPEST_MAX_PCT.
#
# ppd_owned: True means power-profiles-daemon manages it -> read-only for us.
#
# clamped: True means the kernel may report back a value different from what
#      we wrote (rounding / clamping), so self-test must not demand equality.

